& [DependencyCapability] is permission for a crate and feature topology to exist in a selected build
& [ValidatorExecution] is one invocation of compiled schema logic against one in-memory schema or instance
& [ProductionValidation] is a callable Cantor behavior accepting supplied instance material
& [ActivationCandidate] is a reviewed exact proposal that remains non-authoritative until its gate state permits a satisfaction signature
& [ActivationSignature] is the atomic transition authorizing only the signed source touch and behavior
  + none exists in this candidate package

& [TrustedSchema] is one of the five exact checked-in I02 canonical documents after byte digest identity dialect direction closure and bundle lineage verification
& [ProbeInstance] is one source-controlled bounded test value declared inside the focused dependency test
& [UntrustedInstance] is any externally supplied or mutable instance and remains outside I03A

& [NoResolution] has three non-substitutable layers
  + manifest layer disables all default validator features
  + resolved graph layer contains no resolver feature or transport dependency
  + construction layer installs no retriever registry resource loader callback or ambient source
  + local-fragment preflight is later production defense and the focused test exercises its underlying denial assumptions without exporting it

& [Offline] describes availability of dependency and execution inputs without network access
  + offline does not mean resolver capability is absent
& [NoExternalEffect] means no filesystem network registry environment provider model subprocess persistence notification or device interaction occurs in the probe
  + compiler and operating-system reads needed to build admitted local sources are build activity and must not be confused with runtime validator retrieval

& [LockAuthority] binds exact name version source checksum and feature resolution for every package
  + direct manifest exactness alone does not freeze compatible transitive patches
  + the admitted checkpoint must retain jsonschema jsonschema-regex jsonschema-value and referencing at 0.49.2
  + the ignored probe lock is evidence of feasibility only and never the production lock

& [HostAdmission] means the actual operating system permits every required build helper and test harness to execute
  + compile completion cannot be inferred when a helper was denied before execution
  + debug host admission does not imply release host admission
  + later admission without source change may close the gate but must preserve the earlier fault

& [FeatureTopology] is closed
  + cantor_procedure_tool default is empty
  + json-schema enables schemars generation only
  + schema-conformance enables json-schema and dep:jsonschema
  + no other workspace crate gains a dependency edge or feature edge

& [ProbeBoundary] is compile and test evidence rather than library API
  + test observes exact document meta-validity compilation local instance results external-reference refusal numeric boundary and deterministic repeat
  + test constructs no public form and emits no persistent generated artifact
  + engine diagnostic strings are never asserted as stable semantic identity

& [FailureMeaning] is atomic refusal
  + dependency drift resolver capability host denial audit fault test mismatch resource exhaustion or evidence staleness prevents activation
  + partial passing observations remain evidence but grant no source mutation authority

& [RefinedDisposition] is exact_unsigned_optional_test_capability_candidate
